From 2edffc37b8d352a5b44770d9780ace83abab4e7a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adrien Delmas <adrien@adriendelmas.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 10:35:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 142/144] hydra: the Houdini package finds the plugin next to
 itself, not at the build prefix

cycles.json carried CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX, so the file written by a build
held the absolute path of the machine that built it (a drive letter, a user
folder). Copied to another machine it loaded nothing, with no message.

CYCLES_ROOT is now built from $HOUDINI_PACKAGE_PATH, the folder Houdini
resolves to that of the package file being read:

    packages/cycles.json
    packages/CyclesForHoudini/houdini/...

so the pair can be dropped into any packages folder and moved afterwards.
tools/make_dist.py assembles that layout from an install tree.

Checked: a copy of the pair in a scratch HOUDINI_USER_PREF_DIR, hython
22.0.368 resolves CYCLES_ROOT to the copy, loads cycles_vops.hda and lists
HdCyclesPlugin and HdCyclesPluginGPU among the renderer plugins.
---
 src/hydra/resources/cycles.json.in | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/hydra/resources/cycles.json.in b/src/hydra/resources/cycles.json.in
index 5e1636df..f3a7b3c0 100644
--- a/src/hydra/resources/cycles.json.in
+++ b/src/hydra/resources/cycles.json.in
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@
   "env": [
     {
       "CYCLES_ROOT": {
-        "value": "@CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX@/houdini",
+        "value": "$HOUDINI_PACKAGE_PATH/CyclesForHoudini/houdini",
         "method": "replace"
       }
     },
